data.github#GitHub:
The app runs the GitHub device flow: it shows a code and the page where to enter it, and opens that page in the browser. Only a client ID is needed on the device, so create a GitHub OAuth App with Device Flow enabled, put its ID in github_client_id, and its client secret in the file provider--secret. The app asks for read:user, user:email and read:org.
The server first asks GitHub, with that secret, whether the token was minted by that OAuth app (only those are admitted), then resolves the person through the GitHub API: their numeric ID is the subject (github:), their organisations (/user/orgs) are their groups for tenants, and their public email, when they have one, counts as verified. With allowed_orgs, an active membership of one of those organisations admits them, and so does being a named members entry of a tenant (pinned to the account ID, see tenants). The list is optional only when a tenant has members: with neither, the server refuses to start, and so it does without a client ID or without the secret file. Set api_url for GitHub Enterprise.
{"id":"hub","kind":"github","name":"GitHub","github_client_id":"Iv1.0123456789abcdef","allowed_orgs":["my-org","my-other-org"]}

data.openid-connect#OpenID Connect:
kind oidc with oidc_issuer (discovered through /.well-known/openid-configuration) and oidc_client_id, the audience the ID token must carry. The app runs the authorization code flow with PKCE: it opens the browser and receives the redirect on http://127.0.0.1:/callback, with a port chosen at each sign-in. It asks for openid profile email offline_access. Register a public/native client, without a secret, so this kind has no secret file.
The server takes the subject, the email and email_verified, the preferred_username and the groups claim (a list, or a single string). With allowed_domains, the email’s domain must be one of those, and the email must be verified.
{"id":"campus","kind":"oidc","name":"Campus","oidc_issuer":"https://idp.example.org","oidc_client_id":"claimward","allowed_domains":["example.org"]}
